{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01GaGDt4SSqXEXnkGrUYgPzp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A single-user personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`, no syncing/siblings). Plain-markdown files are the source of truth â€” `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files (`academic/commercial/family/writing`), plus archive files for cancelled/saved tasks. No database, no binary formats.\n\n- **It ships as a local web app** (`anchor_gui.py`) â€” a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server bound to `http://localhost:8777`, run persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. It generates the full dashboard HTML on each request and reads/writes the markdown directly, so task add/done/capture/edit happen live in the browser. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) does the same operations and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core capability = GTD-style task lifecycle:** tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, with priority/energy/domain/due/notes fields, organized into per-domain views.\n\n- **It has grown a substantial \"R&D Control Surface\"** â€” a mission-control for trio-driven (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) project work, built in four versions (v2â€“v4, all merged to master). This turns each project into a cockpit window with per-lane session tiles, status lights, cached/validated AI summaries, cost/token/time rollups, a grass-idea board, and deliverable launch-by-type.\n\n- **v3/v4 added real interactive terminals:** worktree-isolated **ConPTY sessions** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket + SSE fallback) where opening a session auto-loads the lane's skill once and greets once, with an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini, Gemini research-only). `pywinpty` is the *one* declared native dependency (lazy, optional, terminal-only); everything else stays stdlib.\n\n- **Reliability is enforced by a daily 5 AM health check** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that parses every file, boots a throwaway server, and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never touching the live `:8777` service or real data), writing dated reports and flagging failures with a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **Branded as a Ghost World Labs tool** \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" with a vendored brand mark serving as favicon and masthead lockup.\n\nThis is grounded in the project's `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North-Star/decision anchors from the rnd-v3/v4 planning docs. Want me to verify any specific claim against the actual code rather than the docs?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24733,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24733},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"534f21f8-8794-4b85-ad3b-838b21e4738a","uuid":"8ac62f67-1521-4799-878e-4d9241b0a5de","request_id":"req_011Cc1v29Z7UcTMeS6vmcSdc"}
